```

But `@ValueSource(strings=...)` only provides ONE argument. The `{1}` placeholder won't have a value, and the method signature has TWO parameters but `@ValueSource` only provides one. The TestInfo is auto-injectable but the `{1}` in the name won't resolve.

Let me fix this — simpler is better. Just use `{0}` (the URL) and drop the TestInfo. Or even simpler: use `{0}` for the URL.

